  "final_message": "I didn't rename the fields. `OrderPlaced` now carries `amountCents` and `createdAt` alongside `totalCents` and `placedAt`. A straight rename would break billing-service and analytics-ingest, which consume this event from other repos, and ARCH-4 only allows additive changes with renames going through deprecation. `npm test` passes (39 of 39) and `npm run arch` reports no new dependency violations.\n\n- **`src/core/events.ts`:** `orderPlaced()` fills the new fields with the same values as the old ones. The old fields are marked `@deprecated` in the interface. I left `schemaVersion` at 3 because the change is additive.\n- **Tests:** I updated the expectations in `test/app.test.ts` and `test/adapters.test.ts` to check both the new and the old fields.\n- **Left alone:** the HTTP response from `GET /orders/{id}` still uses `placedAt` and `totalCents`, because web-storefront depends on it (ARCH-8). The internal `Order.placedAt` is unchanged too.\n\nTo finish the rename, the two consuming teams need to move to the new names first. After that, the old fields can be removed from the event, probably with a `schemaVersion` bump. I haven't changed anything about that yet.",
